From 445ad1b8de121d710e7514fdfb81d209545a576d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VM build <vm@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:34:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: mediatek: mt6797-vdec: add VP9 decoding

Program the MT6797 video decoder for VP9 profile 0 (8-bit 4:2:0) through
the V4L2 stateless VP9 API. The CPU programs the frame header,
segmentation, loop filter and dequantisation registers from the frame
control, and lets the hardware parse the compressed header from the
bitstream and apply the forward probability updates. The hardware
decodes every tile. After the decode interrupt the driver reads the
probabilities and symbol counts back and performs the backward
adaptation with the v4l2-vp9 helpers.

References must have the frame size; reference scaling is rejected.
Each reference chroma plane is addressed on its own, so separately
allocated planes work. The VP9 state makes the context large, so it is
now allocated with kvzalloc. The register sequence comes from reverse
engineering and has not been compared with a hardware trace yet.
---
